WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.953
Movies have the power to
connect people by common ground.

00:00:05.953 --> 00:00:07.870
I might not know something
about someone else,

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:09.420
and by watching
this movie, I get

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.640
to connect with whoever
made this movie and whatever

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.765
story that they're telling.

00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:15.150
They are something that
you can identify with,

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.480
and you can connect with it just
like you can with anyone else.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.480
It's movies that
really have the power

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.430
to connect people with ideas
and connect people with others

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.500
who are not like them.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.205
Movies are powerful
tools for empathy.

00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:32.580
I think it's the
closest thing we

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.640
have to be able to see the world
through someone else's eyes.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.130
You can experience other
cultures, other circumstances,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.420
other places.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.000
Places that you've never
been, you may never go.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.320
It's really about reminding
us that we're all one,

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.590
and that we all go through
the same pains and joys

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.060
and struggles.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:01:07.830
[SPEAKING SPANISH]

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.860
The one thing I love is when
you go to a movie theater

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.530
and you feel the
emotion from the screen

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.850
sweep over the audience.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.760
The way that that
crowd almost becomes

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.010
like one living
being you're a part

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.630
of that's absorbing this movie.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.440
That is so important, I
think, for human beings.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.940
Movies have given people
sanity during this really

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.360
unprecedented time.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.270
And it gave me a sense of pride
to be a part of something that

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.300
helps people come together and
keeps their families feeling

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.020
a sense of normalcy.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.980
I really have come to love films
that bring families together.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.470
And I've tried to do that
with most of my films.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.590
I try to make stories that
both children, their parents,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.960
and their parents' parents
can all appreciate.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.750
On different levels, but
all together as a family.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:59.660
Movies have the power to unite.

